hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2738","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar (Bundar), who narrated to us Yahya, i.e., Yahya ibn Sa'id, who narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qiddah. And narrated to us Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Zaydah. And narrated to us Yahya ibn Hakim, who narrated to us Makki ibn Ibrahim. And narrated to us Salam ibn Junadah, who narrated to us Waki', from Sufyan. All of these chains of narration report the hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who narrated from al-Qasim, from Aishah (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The stoning of the Jamarat and Tawaf around the Sacred House (the Kaaba) were prescribed only to establish the remembrance of Allah"","" and not for any other purpose.\"" This is the end of the narration as reported by Muhammad ibn Bashshar (Bundar). The other narrators added the following phrase to the hadith: \""and the Sa'i (ritual walking) between Safa and Marwah.\"""""""
